cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the latest version of the Zenodo record, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24139477. Version 1 is superseded; its known errors are listed in ERRATA.md."
title: "Two horizon Ruppeiner geometry of level homogeneous black hole entropies (article and replay script)"
abstract: "A short article and the script that replays each of its statements. For entropies of the form S = W(M) s(J/W(M)), with an arbitrary level function W, the Ruppeiner metric is diagonal in the coordinates (M, J/W) and the product of scalar curvature and entropy depends on W through one scale invariant combination only. For the two branch family S = 2 pi (W +/- sqrt(W^2 - J^2)) the sum of R S over the two horizons equals -1 for every level function, and an exact converse characterizes the entropy products for which this holds. The record also contains version 1 of this work (July 2026), which is superseded, with its errata."
